        "evidence": "Recomputed everything quoted. trace T_pn = h/2 - h/2 = 0 and det T_pn = -(h/2)^2 - 1 = -(1 + h^2/4), both as printed. [2]_q^2/4 = (q+q^-1)^2/4 evaluates to 1.0109265521 at the proton pin q0 = 1.1099785827513808 and 1.0109265546 at the muon pin 1.10997859555733471, so \"approximately 1.011\" is right and - worth recording - this quantity cannot discriminate the two pins, which differ only in the 9th significant figure of the result. \"The square of half the quantum 2-integer\" is the correct reading of [2]_q^2/4. The one strong claim, \"All nuclear binding energy arises from the mixed (pn) crossings\", is explicitly conditioned on the interleaved ground-state ordering in the sentence before it."
